AS(1)

NAME
     as - the 68030 assembler

SYNOPSIS
     as [-o out] [-f elf|bin] [-I dir] [-D name[=value]] file.s

DESCRIPTION
     as (azas) assembles Motorola-syntax 68030, 68881/68882 and 68851
     PMMU code into an ELF object file (or a flat binary with -f bin).

     Syntax
       label:          a label (a label in column 0 needs no colon)
       .local          a local label, scoped to the previous label
       ; comment       also * in column 0
       123 $7F 0x7F %1010 @17 'c'    numbers; * is the current address
       move.l d0,(a0)+               mnemonic.size operands

     Directives
       section name   text data bss rodata   select a section
       xdef / global  export symbols;  xref  declare imports
       dc.b/.w/.l     data ("strings" in dc.b);  ds.b/.w/.l n  space
       dcb.x n,v      n copies;  even  align n  cnop off,n  alignment
       equ  set  =    symbols;  org  (binary output)
       include "f"    incbin "f"
       macro / endm   \1..\9 arguments, \@ unique label, narg
       rept n / endr  repeat;  if / ifdef / ifndef / else / endif
       end

     Branches without a size are sized automatically.

SYSTEM CALLS
     trap #0 with the call number in d0 and arguments in d1-d5. See
     intro(2) and /usr/src/examples/hello.s.

SEE ALSO
     ld(1), cc(1), intro(2)
